   - Explicitly state the veracity of the claim (supported, refuted, partially correct, or unverifiable) based on the evidence.
   - Correct any misinformation, misattributions, or conflations in the claim (e.g., confusing actors with similar names, misclassifying film genres, or inaccurate habitat attributions).
   - Where the claim is ambiguous, incomplete, or partially accurate, provide clear evidence-backed clarifications or distinctions.
